author ai
file crates/ui/src/tree.rs
symbol place
lines 0 44
hash 19cbe1865a8f07ba
note Positions, top-down: an element's rectangle comes from the position its parent gave it, its clip is its parent's clip narrowed by the parent's own rectangle, so nothing ever draws or takes a click outside any of its ancestors, and then it walks a cursor along its own direction placing its children, applying the cross-axis alignment and subtracting the scroll offset. The extent the cursor reached along the direction, or the width the children had before they were squeezed when that is larger, and the widest child (at least the element's own size) across it, are stored as the content size: the next frame clamps a scroll against it on each axis, and a view reads it to tell whether a row fits. A floating child is placed at its own absolute position and clipped only by the screen.

