note How an element lays its children out: direction, a size per axis, padding, gap, cross-axis alignment, a scroll offset applied to the children, the axes it shows a scrollbar on and scrolls along (ScrollAxes, vertical unless asked), and a floating absolute position that takes it out of the parent's flow and onto the upper layer. There is no separate clip flag: an element clips exactly when it scrolls.

