author ai
file crates/ui/src/tree.rs
symbol grow
lines 0 51
hash cdd5d8d9176a43fe
note Grow, top-down: a root or a floating element grows to the window, and a floating element that fits its content stops at the window's right edge. Then each parent splits whatever it has left after its non-growing children equally among its growing ones along its direction (a growing child never gets less than its least width), gives them the full inner size across it, and squeezes its children horizontally when they still do not fit. Only widths are squeezed: a column taller than its parent is content to scroll, a row wider than its panel is text that would run past the panel's edge.

