note The track and thumb of a scrollbar along one axis, for a rectangle, the part of it that shows, the content's length on that axis and the scroll offset, or None when the content fits. A vertical track runs down the rectangle's right edge; a horizontal one along the bottom of the part that shows, so an element taller than its viewport still shows its bar, though never above the element's own top. The thumb is proportional with a minimum length. The same geometry is painted by draw_scrollbars and hit-tested by drag_scrollbar and on_scrollbar, so they cannot disagree.

