file crates/ui/src/tree.rs
symbol fit
lines 0 39
hash 0adeba3436bd26d7
note Fit, bottom-up: children first, then a parent's fitting size is the sum of its in-flow children along its direction and the largest across it, plus padding and gaps. Exact is taken as given and Grow counts as zero until the grow pass. A fitted-height element that scrolls sideways and overflows grows by one bar width (scrollbar_room), so its bar does not cover its last row. The same pass sums the least size each element can be squeezed to (least_leaf for a childless one): an exact element's least is its size, a fitting one's is capped at its fitting size, and a growing one keeps its content's least so the grow pass can hand it at least that much.

