note The tree itself: roots, the stack of elements still open (the top is the one being filled), and last frame's Placement per id - that map is the whole of what survives a frame, and it is what every hit test and every scroll clamp reads. hot is the id under the mouse, active the id the left button went down on and is still held over, last_mouse turns the pointer into a drag delta, scroll_drag holds the id whose scrollbar thumb is being dragged the axis and how far along the thumb the mouse grabbed it, and pointer and size are this frame's copy of the input's pointer and the window size.

